※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4932 LANG_EMPTY_WRITTEN

※ An arena a body made is given back when the block it was defined in is left,
※ on every way out, so there is nothing for a program to give back and no
※ `⎕empty` to write.  One wanted afresh for every turn of a loop is defined in
※ the loop.
let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let scratch: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let both: str = "a" ⧺ "b" in scratch
    let n: u64 ¤size = #both
    ⎕empty(scratch)
    if n = 2: 0u6 else: 1u6
